&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trust is central to Stripe’s mission to grow the GDP of the internet and the Risk team advances that mission by building products and infrastructure that Stripe businesses, Stripe product teams, and Stripe’s network of regulators and financial partners rely on. From helping businesses onboard to Stripe to managing regulatory compliance at scale, Risk is at the center of what makes Stripe run. The Technical Program Manager team is responsible for delivering the cross-Stripe programs that help businesses grow on Stripe, enable products to launch safely at scale, and Stripe to maintain its position as the most trusted network in the financial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of TPMs and PGMs to deliver on Stripe’s most complex, cross-cutting, and critical programs. As a manager, you will support your team in leading programs that advance Stripe and Risk’s mission. You’ll hire, coach, and grow a team of excellent TPMs that support Stripe’s growing needs and the individuals’ careers. You will also act as a TPM yourself on the most complex initiatives that uniquely need your hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and manage high-performing teams, managers, and individuals, across multiple locations, including providing performance reviews, continual feedback, and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and deliver on long-term vision and multi-year strategy for company-wide programs collaborating with product management and engineering leadership/executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success criteria, delivery plans, track risks, and ensure successful execution of Risk’s most complex programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make substantial improvements to how the teams you work with communicate and operate to significantly increase the productivity and efficiency of the teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of management experience of varying seniority, including managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering, systems engineering or technical product/program management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in finding and growing talent through coaching, mentoring, and career development conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical programs from ideation to delivery at scale and leading teams of Technical Program Managers who have done the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating autonomously and leading across multiple teams, with stakeholders in different disciplines across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to demonstrate critical thinking and thought leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed teams that designed and operated critical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe’s organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience as an engineer or similar technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marketing Operations is a team of marketing execution experts and systems thinkers focused on efficiency. We partner closely with Regional and Demand marketing, Growth, Martech, and creative teams to deliver scalable, high-impact campaigns across channels. While we operate globally, this role is focused on supporting the EMEA region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Marketing Operations Program Manager to serve as the end-to-end marketing operations process owner for in-person and online events. In this role, you will collaborate with Field Marketing, Demand Generation, Marketing Technology, and Marketing Operations teammates to identify audiences, track and drive attendance, produce high-performing and measurable campaigns, accurately process attendee and non-attendee data, route leads accurately and quickly, and provide sales follow-up reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end marketing operations for in-person and online events, from campaign intake through post-event reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Field Marketing, Demand Generation, Marketing Technology, and Sales to define operational plans, timelines, responsibilities, and success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage audience strategy and campaign execution, including segmentation, registration, email, testing, launch readiness, and attendance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor registration and attendance, address risks and dependencies, and identify opportunities to improve conversion and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the accurate capture, validation, enrichment, and reconciliation of attendee and non-attendee data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee lead scoring, classification, routing, nurture, sales notifications, and handoff within agreed service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on campaign performance, attendance, engagement, lead routing, sales follow-up, and pipeline impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards for data quality, privacy, consent, and contact governance throughout the campaign lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address process, data, and technology gaps by implementing scalable documentation and operating procedures that improve consistency and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in marketing operations, demand generation operations, event operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of proven expertise in Marketo, with a strong track record of developing scalable programs and driving successful campaign outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of optimizing campaign and execution workflows within event and webinar platforms (such as Splash and ON24).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with audience segmentation, campaign workflows, lead management, and sales follow-up processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program-management skills, with the ability to manage timelines, dependencies, risks, and multiple concurrent events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including experience using campaign data to identify issues and improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of data quality, consent, privacy, and contact-governance practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills and experience working across Marketing, Sales, and Technology teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail and the ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment with changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating AI into scalable marketing operations workflow designs and streamline processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology or financial services sectors, ideally within a high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of marketing automation tools and processes to enhance efficiency and scalability in campaign execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong adaptive skills with a proven ability to thrive in a rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or collaborating with an offshore production team to streamline operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Connect Platform&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It helps platforms onboard and verify participants, manage accounts, accept payments, and pay out funds without building payments, compliance, or financial services infrastructure themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Risk team builds the risk management capabilities that help platforms operate safely from day one, including onboarding, Know Your Customer (KYC) verification, fraud and credit risk management, and tax reporting. As AI-native platforms and marketplaces emerge, this work helps Stripe support increasingly dynamic global ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own Connected Account Onboarding Experiences, the products and journeys that help platforms onboard their users safely, compliantly, and with minimal friction. You will shape experiences from sign-up and authentication through readiness to use Stripe products, across application programming interfaces (APIs) and hosted or embedded user interfaces (UI).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will use funnel data, user research, and experimentation to improve conversion while meeting Stripe’s commitments to regulators and financial partners. You will set the strategy for what should be standardized or configurable across platform business models, products, and geographies, including opportunities to use artificial intelligence (AI) and agentic interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision, strategy, goals, and roadmap for Connected Account Onboarding Experiences globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional execution across Connect, Risk, engineering, design, data science, and partner-facing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use funnel metrics, user research, and experimentation to identify friction and improve onboarding conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate risk, regulatory, and partner requirements into intuitive experiences across APIs, platform tools, and connected-account UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable onboarding foundations that support different platform models, geographies, and evolving AI-enabled experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-quarter product roadmaps and aligning internal teams and external partners around shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with engineering, design, and data teams to build products and systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including defining success metrics, running experiments, and using data to improve business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate user problems and product decisions clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on complex platform, ecosystem, or regulated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with autonomy in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high growth companies and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user onboarding solutions in enterprise or business-to-business (B2B) industries through APIs or user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience redesigning traditional user journeys through AI and building agentic interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From having their phone buzz as their first payment comes in to quickly resolving customer issues on-the-go, the Stripe mobile app is a critical lifeline for founders and business owners around the world. Our team is responsible for both the app platform and user-facing experiences. We collaborate closely with every product team to represent, shape, and enhance what it means to be mobile. The next chapter of our mobile efforts will take the quality bar to even greater heights and redefine mobile money movement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a passionate product leader to shape the strategy, amplify its impact across the company, and accelerate Stripe’s mission to help internet businesses grow faster.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the product manager on the Mobile team, you will be accountable for making the mobile app indispensable for startup founders and business owners. How do we get every YC founder to use the app? How can we increase usage across different geographies? How can we get more product teams to contribute to the app? In other words, your role is to ensure founders and business owners are more successful when they use the mobile app.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Deeply understand the needs of founders and business owners and identify the unique superpowers mobile can deliver for them&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Articulate the mobile strategy, prioritize the roadmap, and furiously execute to deliver user value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Craft powerful product experiences with surprisingly great details &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Steer the broader organization to understand and build for mobile use cases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with the go-to-market team to ensure the mobile app is discoverable and compelling&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;8+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Persistence and a whatever-it-takes approach to ensure that your product is successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of user interface (UI) and user experience (UX) principles and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Technical familiarity with mobile development, cross-platform architectures, and machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to collaborate with engineering and design across time zones (PST, EST, CET)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Founder background, or experience in a very early stage company environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Built award-winning mobile apps in the past&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Believe that fast software is the best software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a defining opportunity for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own how every Samsara device comes to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara ships &lt;strong&gt;hundreds of thousands of devices a year&lt;/strong&gt; to fleets, construction sites, and depots worldwide. A single customer rollout can exceed &lt;strong&gt;50,000 devices&lt;/strong&gt;, where every minute saved per install compounds into weeks of deployment time. Each device has a five-minute window where it goes from a box in someone&#39;s hands to a live sensor feeding a customer&#39;s operation. You will own those five minutes and the multi-year vision for what they become.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The install experience is critical to the compounding value of every Samsara product.&lt;/strong&gt; A camera aimed correctly on day one trains better safety models. A gateway reporting cleanly makes every downstream workflow trustworthy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the software install experience end to end, with a dedicated engineering and design team, and you will own one number: &lt;strong&gt;install correctness&lt;/strong&gt;, the share of installs completed right on the first attempt. Correctness today swings by several points depending on whether the installer uses the Samsara Fleet App, and closing that gap for every install is the first prize. Your target is an install under &lt;strong&gt;five minutes of active app time&lt;/strong&gt; that confirms its own health before the installer walks away.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are building for two people who each get the same five minutes. A contracted technician on their twentieth install of the day wants speed. A customer&#39;s shop mechanic on their first wants guidance that assumes nothing. Both are standing in a truck bay, holding a phone, sometimes without signal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand the scale of this problem, review the Samsara Vehicle Gateway &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/products/models/vehicle-gateway&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;, our full hardware lineup &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/products/models&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;, and our installer partner network &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/resources/experts&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote position open to candidates residing in the US.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; Your efforts will result in real-world impact, helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, reduce emissions, and most importantly, ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; If you put in the work, this role won&#39;t be your last at Samsara. We set up our employees for success and have built a culture that encourages rapid career development, countless opportunities to experiment and master your craft in a hyper growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re energized by our opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; The vision we have to digitize large sectors of the global economy requires your full focus and best efforts to bring forth creative, ambitious ideas for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; At Samsara, we win together, celebrate together and support each other. You will be surrounded by a high-calibre team that will encourage you to do your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the three-year vision for device installation and provisioning&lt;/strong&gt;, defining how Samsara hardware comes online as the platform expands across new products, device types, and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own install correctness.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the target, instrument the funnel so every outcome is attributable, and move the number quarter over quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the guided install and verification flow&lt;/strong&gt; in the Samsara Fleet app, for professional installers and for customers who install hardware themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the intelligence that verifies an install is correct&lt;/strong&gt;, checking camera aim, wiring, and signal quality while the installer is still standing at the vehicle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give operations leaders a live view of fleet readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; what is installed, what is verified, and what is producing data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ride along on installs and run sessions in customer yards&lt;/strong&gt;, then turn what you observe into roadmap that shapes hardware, firmware, and software decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara&#39;s cultural principles as we scale globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of product management experience shipping products used by external customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A record of owning a business or product metric and changing its trajectory&lt;/strong&gt;, with a before and after you can walk us through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building something from zero to one&lt;/strong&gt; without a spec, a defined customer, or a playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth sufficient for engineers to treat you as a peer:&lt;/strong&gt; a degree in Computer Science or Engineering, prior experience as an engineer, or demonstrated fluency in system architecture trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate at both altitudes, setting multi-year direction and reviewing the details of a screen flow in the same week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive-level communication and presence, comfortable presenting and defending strategy to the CEO, CPO, and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in a North American time zone. We will consider strong candidates in Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We do not require prior experience with hardware, vehicles, telematics, or field installation. We hire for technical depth, evidence of building from zero to one, and a record of owning a number and moving it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building mobile products for people who work with their hands, in loud, time-pressured, or offline conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of primary research, with specific examples of what watching a customer taught you that a dashboard could not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work on products where software and hardware depend on each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience instrumenting a funnel and running experiments against it.&lt;/li&gt;
